                "Operating across international borders subjects the enterprise to the conflicting jurisdictions of sovereign legal traditions. International marketers cannot operate under the naive assumption that home-country commercial laws apply globally. International legal disputes are adjudicated under three primary legal systems:",
                "1. Common Law Tradition: Rooted in English jurisprudence (practiced in the United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, and India). Common law is based on judicial precedent, past court rulings, and custom. Contracts in common law jurisdictions are extraordinarily detailed, lengthy, and explicit, attempting to anticipate every possible future contingency.",
                "2. Civil Law (Code Law) Tradition: Derived from Roman law and the Napoleonic Code (practiced in over seventy nations across continental Europe, Latin America, and Japan). Civil law is based on comprehensive, codified statutes enacted by national legislatures. Contracts in civil law jurisdictions are substantially shorter because commercial codes automatically supply standardized statutory rules.",
